The `release-binaries` workflow failed for tag 0.504 (2026-10-27, the latest run of that workflow) on x86_64 and aarch64, step "Verify binary". Run: `gh run view 40557655238 -R Getty/langertha-raider --log-failed`.

    Langertha::Engine::AKIOpenAI: Can't locate XS/Parse/Infix.pm in @INC (@INC entries checked: .../archive/lib) at .../archive/lib/DynaLoader.pm line 223.
    FAIL: packed module set

An XS module loaded at run time (`XS::Parse::Infix`, pulled in by a syntax module the engine classes use) is missing from the packed archive, so the release 0.504 has no working binaries attached.

## Steps

1. Find what loads `XS::Parse::Infix` (`perl -MLangertha::Engine::AKIOpenAI -e 'print join "\n", grep /Parse/, keys %INC'`) and add it, with its shared object, to the binary build's module list.
2. Run the binary build and the "packed module set" check locally the way the workflow does.
3. Say on the card whether the 0.504 binaries should be rebuilt on the tag or whether the next release carries the fix; that choice is the maintainer's.

## Proof

The packed-module check passes locally for every engine class, and the workflow's next run is green.
